{"chunk_id": "e1f82543752c", "text": "This section recounts the downfall of Yavakri, illustrating the dangers of pride gained through boons and ascetic power. After obtaining supernatural knowledge of the Vedas, Yavakri\u2019s father Bharadwaja warns him through the tale of Medhavi, a youth whose arrogance after receiving a divine boon led to his death when the condition sustaining his life was destroyed. Ignoring the warning, Yavakri grows reckless and insults other sages. When he lustfully approaches the daughter\u2011in\u2011law of the powerful sage Raivya, she cleverly reports the offense. Enraged, Raivya creates from his matted hair a woman and a demon through sacrificial rites and sends them to kill Yavakri. Deprived of ritual purity and divine protection, Yavakri is hunted, denied refuge, and slain by the demon\u2019s spear. The episode underscores a central epic theme: spiritual power without humility leads inevitably to ruin.\nProud Yavakri ignores warnings, insults Raivya\u2019s family, and is killed by a demon conjured through the sage\u2019s wrathful ritual.\nThemes: pride and downfall, ascetic power, curse and retribution, fate vs effort, sexual misconduct", "vector": [0.0028878776356577873, -0.024512743577361107, 0.017491504549980164, 0.0015491547528654337, -0.004762945231050253, 0.023308319970965385, -0.023157767951488495, -0.03306688368320465, -0.00962853990495205, -0.030986515805125237, 0.010121257975697517, -0.0001692650403128937, 0.020872101187705994, 0.0026124343276023865, -0.012728559784591198, 0.01022390741854906, 0.05094161257147789, -0.02199440449476242, 0.04105987027287483, -0.016574501991271973, 0.0006321509135887027, 0.010579760186374187, 0.0030110571533441544, 0.018353762105107307, -0.01816214993596077, 0.007308656815439463, 0.0020444393157958984, -0.031917206943035126, 0.011195657774806023, -0.007883494719862938, -0.015315331518650055, -0.00588866975158453, 0.017737863585352898, -0.009122134186327457, -0.0338333323597908, 0.0010299184359